Id: cont006i
Severity: INFO
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
References: docker-run(1) --network
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-6, CM-7; ISO 8.2, 8.9; CE Secure configuration, User access control

A running container shares the host's network namespace
(--network=host): its services listen on the host's own addresses, so
the host's firewall, not Docker's port publishing, decides who reaches
them, and it can see all of the host's network traffic on its
interfaces and connect to services the host keeps on 127.0.0.1. Some
software needs it (multicast discovery, home automation); this is
informational.
